## Local conventions

Record replacement and rollback implications for proposed resources. Keep version pins in the existing repository version sources.
Apply these conventions only here; inspect deeper guidance before working there.

## Commands and verification

Review changed Markdown and its relative links using the [fixture guide](../README.md).
No setup, startup, build, or stack test applies: this fixture has no application.
Do not invent a command; an actual adoption must cite its own command sources,
working directories, prerequisites, side effects, and check selection.

## Constraints

No infrastructure is provisioned in this synthetic example. Plan/apply operations require the project's reviewed deployment path.
Respect higher-priority instructions, existing authorization, and permissions.
This guidance grants no authority and is not a security boundary. Report
unresolved conflicts and continue unaffected work without repeated approvals.

## Maintenance

The synthetic fixture maintainer owns this example. Follow the
[fixture update and rollback procedure](../README.md). Keep within 4 KiB UTF-8;
version 1.0.0 records ancestry. Adapt through review, never auto-synchronize.
Verify changes or restoration in a fresh task and preserve unrelated work.
